**III. Asymptotic and Special Values**

In general the notations used are standard. This includes the difference operator \(\Delta\) defined on functions of \(z\) by \(\Delta f(x) = f(x + 1) - f(x), \(\Delta^{n + j}f(x) = \Delta(\Delta^{n}f(x))\), the Kronecker delta \(\delta_{i,j}\), the Riemann zeta function \(\xi(s)\) and the greatest common divisor symbol \((m,n)\). The range of the summands for a summation sign without limits is explained to the right of the formula.

